From 7f0320a4abac4a21ae651dc41918380119dd6aa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:03:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Tests: custody v2 dashboard against the REAL original vault,
 book and SessionVault (anvil)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

test/custody-v2-dashboard-contract.test.mjs runs the page module over the committed bundle, with its real agreed
reader on two JSON-RPC origins, against:
- the original EnclaveSecretVaultV2 built with the production immutables at 0xE48699B8…, whose code hash equals the
  reviewed production hash;
- EnclaveAddressBook at 0xab21… (administrator impersonated);
- the schema-4 registry and ownership;
- the real SessionVault/SessionVaultFactory;
- a genesis committee from the vault's own createCommittee (n 1, t 1, W 1).

It covers:
- root's exact unsigned activation and rollback calldata;
- EOA save, rotate, pause and resume, with bundles decrypting to the env;
- a session key refused by the page AND by the vault (NotOwner) for the same page calldata;
- a SessionVault deployment refused while the book names no factory, and accepted by the beneficial EOA's DIRECT update
  once the admin sets it;
- the ownerCall route reverting.

A second test pins that the panel's signer is wallet.js's direct send.
The fixture suites are updated for the seat wording, the per-call book check and the SessionVault refusal.
Only the ledger is a stand-in.
---
